<title>JAPAN: Japan's GDP rises 1.6 pct in January-March--EPA.</title>
<headline>Japan's GDP rises 1.6 pct in January-March--EPA.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's gross domestic product (GDP) rose a real 1.6 percent in the January to March quarter from the previous quarter, or an annualised 6.6 percent, the Economic Planning Agency (EPA) said on Friday.  </p>
<p>			JANUARY/MARCH		   PREV QTR</p>
<p> Real GDP	+1.6, annualised +6.6	+0.9, annualised +3.8</p>
<p> Real GNP	+1.7, annualised +6.9	+0.6, annualised +2.4</p>
<p> Nominal GDP   +2.2			     +0.5</p>
<p> Nominal GNP   +2.2			     +0.1</p>
<p> (Annual rate)		JANUARY/MARCH	PREV QTR</p>
<p> GDP deflator		     +0.0 pct	 -0.1 pct</p>
<p>(Real data in percentage of contribution to overall GDP)  Domestic demand		   +1.5	     +0.5</p>
<p>   Private			   +2.6	     +1.2</p>
<p>   Public			    -1.0	     -0.7</p>
<p> External demand		   +0.1	     +0.4</p>
<p>   Exports goods/services	+0.1	     +0.6</p>
<p>   Imports goods/services	-0.0	     -0.2</p>
<p>Breakdown of domestic demand contribution:</p>
<p>Private</p>
<p>   Personal outlays		+2.7	     +0.7</p>
<p>   Housing			   -0.2	     +0.2</p>
<p>   Capital spending		+0.1	     +0.4</p>
<p>   Inventory changes	     -0.0	     -0.1</p>
<p>Public</p>
<p>   Government outlays	    +0.0	     +0.1</p>
<p>   Capital spending		-1.1	     -0.7</p>
<p>   Inventory changes	     +0.0	     -0.0</p>
<p>(Real data - changes in expenditures) Private</p>
<p>   Personal outlays		+4.6	     +1.2</p>
<p>   Housing			   -3.9	     +4.0</p>
<p>   Capital spending		+0.7	     +2.2</p>
<p>   Inventory changes	    -12.9	    -51.6</p>
<p>Public</p>
<p>   Government outlays	    +0.1	     +0.6</p>
<p>   Capital spending	     -12.4	     -7.4</p>
<p>   Inventory changes	   +619.7	    -42.3</p>
<p> External			   +10.3	   +146.5</p>
<p> Exports			     +0.7	     +5.0</p>
<p> Imports			     +0.2	     +1.8</p>
<p>(Note: Due to rounding, figures may not tally. Also, figures smaller than two decimal places are not shown.)</p>
</text>
